LIBPKGBUILD(3)

# NAME

libpkgbuild - sealed logical package-build authority

# SYNOPSIS

*#include <libpkgbuild/libpkgbuild.h>*

# DESCRIPTION

*libpkgbuild* admits one catalog-backed selected package from a complete
*libpkgresolve* result and seals its exact source snapshot, direct build/check
resolver inputs, selected architectures, and closed build policy into an
immutable *build_request*.

A successful *build_result* binds that request, execution evidence, a complete
intended payload, and exact artifact bytes. A failed result binds the request,
execution evidence, and failure evidence and contains no partial success data.

Foreign-bearing request and result values use opaque immutable storage. The
public libpkgbuild ABI therefore does not embed libpkgsource or libpkgresolve
object layouts.

# NON-GOALS

The core does not parse recipe syntax, discover collections, resolve packages,
acquire sources, materialize package trees, execute programs, inspect archives,
project planner facts, publish installed state, or apply payloads.

# SEE ALSO

*pkgbuild_model*(3), *pkgbuild_request*(3), *pkgbuild_result*(3),
*libpkgsource*(3), *libpkgresolve*(3)
